      "writtenOn": "2021-09-23T19:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "any chance for mul to fail for arbitrary x and y (e.g. too small / too big)? if yes, we now risk g2f_individual_key_pair() returning a failure instead of retrying.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "0502aef82c16c20ad634ceaab4e88aeb3e331f46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "caff4cf5_6e946b36",
        "filename": "board/cr50/dcrypto/p256_ec.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-23T22:38:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "dcrypto_p256_base_point_mul() takes d as input and computes (x,y). For valid d (which we check in lines 134-136) it should always produce (x,y). Failure to do it means our P-256 implementation is broken. Same with pair-wise consistency test - if we sign and can\u0027t verify what we got - we have a problem. For many tests I already ran I didn\u0027t face this check to report an error.",
      "parentUuid": "4d6d4ff3_b92228a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "0502aef82c16c20ad634ceaab4e88aeb3e331f46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b28a9d8_40692605",
        "filename": "board/cr50/dcrypto/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 476,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-23T19:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what if it\u0027s neither FAIL nor RETRY nor SUCCESS? we try again w/o doing buf -\u003e sha256(buf).\n\nto be future proof I suggest something like:\n\n```\n\t\twhile(1) {\n\t\t\tresult \u003d DCRYPTO_p256_key_from_bytes(pk_x, pk_y, d,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t     (uint8_t *)buf);\n\t\t\tif (result \u003d\u003d DCRYPTO_SUCCESS)\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t\tif (result !\u003d DCRYPTO_RETRY)\n\t\t\t\treturn false;\n\n\t\t\t// this block below probably deserves being extracted\n\t\t\t// as a method with self-commenting naming\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\tstruct sha256_ctx sha;\n\t\t\t\tSHA256_hw_init(\u0026sha);\n\t\t\t\tSHA256_update(\u0026sha, buf, sizeof(buf));\n\t\t\t\tmemcpy(buf, SHA256_final(\u0026sha), sizeof(buf));\n\t\t\t}\t\t\t\n\t\t}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 476,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 476,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "0502aef82c16c20ad634ceaab4e88aeb3e331f46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
